Z||000004||speed racer||01-31-2001||11:26 PM||||They only made 3 cars for the track that is what I mean all others are replicas||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-31-2001||11:44 PM||||There were originally 5 "Real" Pace cars. One is at the Museum of science and industry in chicago, 2 are at the Indy Museum at the race track, 1 is in the Pontiac Museum and the 5th was given to VP and it's in his private collection. <BR>This is per the Indy Pace car history. I am not exactly sure how accurate it is and it was listed back in 1992. I do know that 5 were built per the Pontiac Performance Plus magazine that shows what they did exactly to make the pace cars.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mope||02-01-2001||09:18 AM||||I was rite!!!<P>I am so cool!<P>m0pe||||reg||10
Z||000007||mrfixit58||02-01-2001||09:24 AM||||If I'm not mistaken, the actual Indy Pace cars were powered by the high performance Super Duty motor as well as special suspension, brakes, wheels and tires and other goodies that were never intended for production.<P>So, when you see a production 84 Indy Pace car, it's really just a weak cosmetic replica of what could have been. Sad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000008||ChadMan||02-01-2001||09:28 AM||||If Indianapolis Motor Speedway still has one or more of the original Pace Cars, they must have it in storage somewhere because it is not on display at the Hall of Fame Museum in the infield.<P>It's the offseason, and nothing much is going on.  Assuming IMS really does have one of the original Pace Cars...if we wrote a nice letter, I wonder if they'd let 20 or 30 of us come to Indy and check it out? ||||reg||5
Z||000009||Oreif||02-01-2001||09:32 AM||||Per Pontiac Performance Plus, The real Pace cars used a 233HP SD4 engine, F-body Brakes, 28mm axle's from a Pontiac 6000, custom made dropped spindles in front, bigger front sway bar and a small rear sway bar, Centerline 16 X 8 wheels, Blisten shocks and struts, and lowering springs in back. The car was 5.7 0 to 60 and top speed of 144mph.||||reg||1
Z||000010||cifc||02-01-2001||09:59 AM||||Here's a couple pictures of the car in the Chicago Museum of Science and Industry.<BR>If it was one of the indy cars it's been repainted since then.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/museum.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||bHooper||02-01-2001||10:53 AM||||when i went to the F1 event, in september, i asked about the Indy's.  they said the only way to see them would be to wright a letter to Tony George (wonderfull, there's not a bigger *******  in american racing) to see if he would allow a visit.<P>they said the only way that would work, is if i was restoring a indy, and used that as a reason.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
